 and their gymnasts, men and women, would quickly become the dominant nation, although the men were soon challenged, and even surpassed for several Olympics, by the Japanese. The women gymnasts were greeted in Helsinki by a full programme, including four apparatus events and, finally, an " [:a {:href "/results/70171"} "individual all-around competition"] ". Further, the women had a seventh event, which would only be contested in 1952 and " [:a {:href "/results/70202"} "1956"] ", the " [:a {:href "/results/70177"} "team portable apparatus all-around"] ". This was somewhat similar to a team rhythmic gymnastics competition."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Soviet dominance in Helsinki can be seen by the medal lists. Overall, they won nine gold medals and 22 medals, with men leading with five golds in eight events and 11 of 26 medals, while the women won four of the seven events and over half of the medals, with 11 of 21."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/70157"} "Individual All-Around, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "19 – 21 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "185"] "\n" [:td {} "29"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/70158"} "Team All-Around, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "19 – 21 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "170"] "\n" [:td {} "23"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/70165"} "Floor Exercise, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "19 – 21 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "185"] "\n" [:td {} "29"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/70166"} "Horse Vault, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "19 – 21 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "185"] "\n" [:td {} "29"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/70167"} "Parallel Bars, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"